2026-09-27T10:27:47.0218881Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0219164Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0219575Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0219976Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0220117Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0220415Z ================
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0220601Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0220831Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0221365Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0221698Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0221868Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0222269Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0222567Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0222802Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0223385Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0224187Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0225150Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0225970Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0226129Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0226887Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0227718Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0228180Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0228679Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0229359Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0229500Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0229791Z ========
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0229982Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0232094Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0234618Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0234989Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0235735Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0236945Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0237951Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0238899Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0321761Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0322636Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0322819Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0323217Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0323647Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0325280Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0327054Z 
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0328028Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0329351Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:27:47.0329656Z 
